{
  "id": "0b0be2ac9a4ad24e",
  "name": "deploykit - slack → linear triage",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## deploykit - Slack inlet\n\n@mention your bot on any message worth tracking; the thread gets sanitized and triaged into Linear (+1 on an existing root cause, or a new ticket), and the bot replies with the result.\n\n**Setup:**\n1. Import the issue-triage core first, then point *Run Issue Triage* at it.\n2. Attach your **Slack** credential to the trigger and the three Slack-touching nodes.\n3. In your Slack app: subscribe to the `app_mention` event with the trigger's webhook URL; scopes `app_mentions:read`, `channels:history`, `channels:read`, `chat:write`.\n4. Convention: name deployment channels `deploy-<customer>` - the customer slug is derived from the channel name.\n5. Activate.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 400
      },
      "id": "22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222200",
      "name": "Setup Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-60, -440]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "trigger": ["app_mention"],
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222201",
      "name": "Slack Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slackTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [0, 0],
      "credentials": {
        "slackApi": {
          "id": "CONFIGURE_ME",
          "name": "Slack account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "channel",
        "operation": "get",
        "channelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "={{ $json.channel }}"
        }
      },
      "id": "22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222202",
      "name": "Get Channel Info",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slack",
      "typeVersion": 2.3,
      "position": [220, 0],
      "credentials": {
        "slackApi": {
          "id": "CONFIGURE_ME",
          "name": "Slack account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "channel",
        "operation": "replies",
        "channelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "={{ $('Slack Trigger').item.json.channel }}"
        },
        "ts": "={{ $('Slack Trigger').item.json.thread_ts || $('Slack Trigger').item.json.ts }}",
        "returnAll": true,
        "filters": {}
      },
      "id": "22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222203",
      "name": "Get Thread",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slack",
      "typeVersion": 2.3,
      "position": [440, 0],
      "credentials": {
        "slackApi": {
          "id": "CONFIGURE_ME",
          "name": "Slack account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const trigger = $('Slack Trigger').first().json;\nconst channel = $('Get Channel Info').first().json;\nconst messages = $input.all().map(i => i.json);\n\nconst text = messages\n  .map(m => `${m.user || m.username || 'unknown'}: ${(m.text || '').replace(/<@[^>]+>/g, '').trim()}`)\n  .filter(line => line.split(': ').slice(1).join(': ').length > 0)\n  .join('\\n');\n\nconst channelName = channel.name || 'unknown';\nconst tsForLink = (trigger.thread_ts || trigger.ts).replace('.', '');\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    source: 'slack',\n    customer: channelName.replace(/^deploy-/, ''),\n    raw_text: text || (trigger.text || '').replace(/<@[^>]+>/g, '').trim(),\n    link: `https://slack.com/archives/${trigger.channel}/p${tsForLink}`,\n    reported_at: new Date(parseFloat(trigger.ts) * 1000).toISOString(),\n  },\n}];"
      },
      "id": "22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222204",
      "name": "Build Report",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [660, 0]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "workflowId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "",
          "cachedResultName": "deploykit - issue triage (core)"
        },
        "mode": "each",
